@subsection Procedures
@deffn Procedure stexi:api-binding name value
Return the API binding as an stexi definition.

NAME (symbol): The name of the binding.  For example, the name of a
variable, the name of a procedure, etc.

VALUE (anything): Any kind of object.  For example, a string, a list, a
procedure, a record, etc.

RETURN VALUE (stexi): An stexi definition corresponding to the type of
VALUE.

@end deffn

@deffn Procedure stexi:api-chapter sections
Return a library API as an stexi chapter.

SECTIONS (list of stexi): A list where every item is an stexi section.

RETURN VALUE (stexi): A chapter documenting a library's API.

@end deffn

@deffn Procedure stexi:module-description module-name
Return the module's commentary or description as stexi.

MODULE-NAME (list of symbols): For example: '(mylib amodule).

RETURN VALUE (stexi): An stexi fragment.

@end deffn

@deffn Procedure stexi:module-section module-name
Return the module documentation as an stexi section.

MODULE-NAME (list of symbols): For example: '(mylib amodule).

RETURN VALUE (stexi): A section documenting a module's API.

@end deffn

@deffn Procedure stexi:procedure-parameters proc
Return the parameters of the given procedure as a string.

PROC (procedure): A procedure object.

RETURN VALUE (string): A string listing the names of all the required,
optional, keyword, and rest of parameters of the procedure.  Default
values for optional and keyword parameters are not included.

@end deffn


